let's take a quick break from  monsterverse  and dive into other monster content here  today we will be listing out the 10  biggest dinosaurs seen in the two  jurassic world  movies the first one and fallen kingdom  so we also have dominion coming up in  the next year and i'm sure there will be  old classics mixed with new hybrid  dinosaurs  that will be seen in the movie but just  to recap on what happened  jurassic world was gigantic it was a  gigantic park built on the remnants of  jurassic park and then the indominus rex  escaped and all hell broke louis on the  island and then  on fallen kingdom dinos was saved and  brought back to the mainland  for auction but managed to escape and  roam everywhere  so let's see the 10 biggest of these  creatures  here on this list number 10  parasaurolophus these are herbivorous  dinosaurs and in that herd  of dinosaurs there would be a member  that would observe the surrounding area  for any threats  to the herd and would alert if there  were any nearby  it is one of the most distinctive  dinosaurs due to its spectacular  tube-like  shaped crest on its head that is up to 2  meters long  the crust is not only for exhibition but  can also produce a wide variety of  sounds  from sharp high-pitched shrieks to  infrasonic bays  parasaurolophus is a peaceful animal  that lives  in herds led by several adult males  standing 4 meters or 13 feet tall 10  meters or 30 feet long  and it weighs 4 to 5 tons  number 9 admontosaurus the advantasaurus  was one of the dinosaurs in the jurassic  world  theme park according to the park website  it existed in the gallimimus valley  it is a herbivore its diet consists of  ferns converse and other vegetation  the ademondosaurus clones oddly didn't  have the fleshy comb  on their heads like the original species  this dino was 3 meters or 10 feet tall  12 to 13 meters or around 40 feet long  and weighed 5 tons  number 8 stegosaurus stegosaurus is  often called the dumbest dinosaur  because of its incredibly small brain  it's the size of a walnut it's easily  one of the best known dinosaurs and is  recognized all over the world  it is the largest and most famous member  of the stigersaur family  it roamed the open plains of the late  jurassic period in what is now north  america  it has a long tail with spikes and rows  of plates on its back  which inspired the design of godzilla it  was 3 meters or 10 feet tall  8.5 meters or 28 feet long and weighed 6  tons number 7 the ankylosaurus  the ankylosaurus clones in isla saurona  had a dark down underbelly with bright  red patches on the eyes  it also had faded stripes of purple on  his body and its armor was black  it was like a tang with lots of thick  bony armor on its body  its back it also had a nasty weapon a  heavy club on the end of its tail  which could swing around and smash into  an attacking dinosaur  ankylosaurus was huge very big  it's a huge armored dinosaur measuring  about 33 to 35 feet long  around 7.5 to 10.7 meters and 6 feet  or 1.8 meters wide 6.6 feet or two  meters tall  and it weighed roughly 6.5 tons  number six the indominus rex the  indominus rex or  i-rex for short is a genetically  modified species of dinosaur created by  engine for by combining the base genome  of a tyrannosaurus  with that of a velociraptor the first  official hybrid created by indian it  contained the genetic material of also  carnotaurus giganotosaurus the  majingosaurus as well as  an assortment of modern species this led  to the birth of a new creature a modern  dinosaur that was a monster  that could regulate body temperature  camouflage itself  solve problems and kill everything in  sight it was 6.1 meters or 20 feet tall  15 meters or 50 feet long and weighed  eight  tons number five tyrannosaurus rex  commonly known as a t-rex this species  lived during the late cretaceous period  in modern day  north america and was therefore among  the last non-avian dinosaurs  like other tyrannosaurus tyrannosaurus  had very short arms with only two  fingers  despite the limb size each were able to  bench press about 400 pounds  this apex predator was notorious for its  powerful bite force  and also its size as as it was 20 feet  tall or 6 meters  40 feet long or 12 meters and weighed  around 9 tons in the movie  the oldest t-rex in the franchise is  rexy the one seen in the first movie the  jurassic park film  and also in the last one in fallen  kingdom  number four triceratops triceratops is  one of the most common dinosaur fossils  found  more than 50 skulls have been found till  date the serotopian family is one of the  most successful and varied  of the late cretaceous triceratops is  the largest member of this family  reaching the size of a school bus it is  quadripedal  has a muscular body and a skull with a  shield-like plate  with three massive horns although it was  short in height and length  than other previous entries it was still  heavier at around 12  tons so it was also 3 meters or 10 feet  tall  and 9 meters or 30 feet long  number three the mosasaurus these apex  predators of the prehistoric deep  can feast on all matter of ocean life  their double hinged jaws  open wide for any prey they could find  in the movies which include placeosaurus  and the great white sharks humans and  also the indominus rex too  they are not actually dinosaurs but in  fact marine reptiles  various estimates for its size was  thrown by fans and the movie makers  alike  the website states it to be 55 feet long  or 16.7 meters  and weighing 28 tons we don't doubt the  weight but  fans argue that the creature was at  least 21 to 24 meters or between 70 and  80 feet long  number two apatosaurus these dinosaurs  are one of the most famous of the giant  jurassic plant eaters  it was a sauropod a member of a race of  huge long neck dinosaurs  it was longer than two school buses and  weighed as much as four adult male  african elephants apotheosaurus is a  fairly typical member of the diplodocus  family  long necks pillar-like legs a long  tapering tail and enormous in size  it had like other family members back  leg teeth in a head  that seemed very small for such a large  creature it was 4.5 meters or 15 feet  tall  23 to 27 meters or between 75 and 90  feet long  and weighed 20 to 36 tons  and number one the brachiosaurus  and so the biggest on this list is yet  again another sauropod long neck  dinosaur  the brachiosaurus it gets its name from  the great height of its humerus  or the upper arm bone which is longer  than most humans at all  the size and high reach of the  brachiosaurus is its protection  only a starving or an insane carnivore  would attack such a huge mountain of  muscle brachiosaurus was one of the  first dinosaurs bred by injen for  jurassic park on isla nubla  and also found on isla sorna as well as  jurassic world  the successor to the first spark it was  13  or 43 feet tall as long as the t-rex  from head to tail  it was 21 meters or around 70 feet long  and weighed  56 tons and so with that we come to the  end of the video  on the 10 biggest dinosaurs from the  jurassic world series of films  which is jurassic world one and jurassic  world the fallen kingdom  we hope to see more on the upcoming  flick which means we want to see more  dinosaurs in the upcoming movie  and yes we will be doing more dinosaur  videos in the days to come  so stay tuned slap that like button  for support smash that subscribe button  to be a part of the mind cue family  and hit that notification bell like a  sunday church bell for regular updates  on dino and monster content till the  next one  take care fam

